    "code": "import math\nfrom scipy.stats import norm\n\ndef solution():\n    # Define variables name and value\n    asset_value = 150.0\n    debt_value = 100.0\n    risk_free_rate = 0.05\n    asset_volatility = 0.20\n    time_to_maturity = 3.0\n\n    # Do math calculation to get the answer\n    d1 = (\n        math.log(asset_value / debt_value)\n        + (risk_free_rate + 0.5 * asset_volatility**2) * time_to_maturity\n    ) / (asset_volatility * math.sqrt(time_to_maturity))\n\n    d2 = d1 - asset_volatility * math.sqrt(time_to_maturity)\n\n    equity_value = (\n        asset_value * norm.cdf(d1)\n        - debt_value\n        * math.exp(-risk_free_rate * time_to_maturity)\n        * norm.cdf(d2)\n    )\n\n    answer = round(equity_value, 2)\n\n    # return answer\n    return answer\n"
